        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Labatt Open\n- Companies: Labatt Brewing Company, Mill Street Brewery, Anheuser–Busch InBev\n- People: John Sharples, Jr.\n- Places: Canada\n- Topics: golf, brewing, politics\n\nFacts:\n- The Labatt Open was a golf event on the PGA Tour that was played in Canada in the mid-1950s.\n- The Labatt Open was sponsored by the Labatt Brewing Company.\n- John Sharples was born on 24 January 1847 and died on 30 July 1913.\n- John Sharples was a Canadian business person and politician.\n- In 2015, Labatt Brewing Company purchased Mill Street Brewery.\n- Labatt Brewing Company is the largest brewer in Canada.\n- Labatt Brewing Company is owned by Anheuser–Busch InBev.",
